``JsonViewer`` displays a JSON file in a :class:`~PySide6.QtWidgets.QTreeView`.
Internally, it loads the contents of a file into a data structure via a string and
uses it to populate a custom tree model with JsonItemModel.

The JSON viewer demonstrates how to implement a custom item model
inherited from :class:`~PySide6.QtCore.QAbstractItemModel`.

``JsonViewer`` uses the top-level objects of the document as bookmarks for
navigation. Other nodes (keys and values) can be added as additional bookmarks,
or removed from the bookmark list. A :class:`~PySide6.QtWidgets.QLineEdit`
is used as a search field to navigate through the JSON tree.
